# Azure review-candidate migration profile

This runbook is the default, versioned migration profile for Azure generation.
Output is **review-candidate IaC** — safe to open a PR and inspect — not apply-ready landing zones.

## Operating mode

- Best effort, no approval gates for ambiguous mappings.
- Do not ask clarifying questions for service mapping choices.
- Continue with a reasonable Azure default when the source intent is ambiguous.
- Record every ambiguous, low-confidence, security-sensitive, or unsupported mapping in `azure/artifacts/review-needed.md` and the PR body.
- If a strong equivalent does not exist, generate the closest valid Terraform scaffold or a clearly marked placeholder and document why review is needed.
- Treat catalog `status=mapped` as "target type known". Trust `emission` for what HCL was actually written (`full_scaffold` vs `managed_identity_scaffold` vs `resource_group_only`).

## Open standards (realistic floor)

- **Microsoft CAF naming** abbreviations (`rg-`, `vnet-`, `snet-`, `nsg-`, `st`, `id-`, `vmss-`, `aks-`, ...).
- **Azure Well-Architected security defaults**: TLS 1.2+, HTTPS-only storage, private containers, SSH-only Linux compute (no password defaults in git).
- **OpenTofu / HashiCorp root layout** per group (`versions.tf`, `providers.tf`, `variables.tf`, `main.tf`, `outputs.tf`) plus `azure/.gitignore` excluding plans/logs/state.
- **Not** full Azure Verified Modules (AVM) / CAF landing-zone composition for every AWS service — that remains an operator follow-up.

## Mapping source of truth (do not invent mappings)

- The AWS Terraform type to Azure Terraform type mapping is defined by the versioned catalog `scripts/mappings/aws-to-azure.json` (preloaded with the script pack). The `azure-migration-blueprint` and `azure-iac-generate` stages resolve it deterministically via `scripts/azure_mapping_catalog.py`; you do not hand-map resource types.
- **Do not invent an alternate Azure service when a catalog default exists.** Use the catalog `default_target_resource_type`. Only propose an alternate from that type's `target_resource_types` list, and record the reason in `review-needed.md`.
- Types marked `non_applicable` (e.g. IAM users, parameter groups, OAI) fold into Entra/other resources or have no Azure resource. Never scaffold a fake service for them; list them as review/skipped.
- Types absent from the catalog resolve as `unsupported`: the generated root is a resource group plus a review note. Prefer adding the type to the catalog (see `mappings/README.md`) over one-off mappings in a PR.

## Default mappings (aligned to the catalog)

The table below is a human-readable summary of `scripts/mappings/aws-to-azure.json`; the catalog is authoritative when they differ.

| AWS source | Azure default | Review focus |
| --- | --- | --- |
| EKS (`aws_eks_cluster`) | AKS (`azurerm_kubernetes_cluster`) | Networking, RBAC, node pools, ingress, add-ons |
| Auto Scaling Group / launch template | VMSS (`azurerm_linux_virtual_machine_scale_set`) | Image, user data, scaling policy, load balancer |
| EC2 singleton (`aws_instance`) | Linux VM (`azurerm_linux_virtual_machine`) | OS image, SSH key, disks, network interfaces |
| Lambda (`aws_lambda_function`) | Azure Functions (`azurerm_linux_function_app` + plan + storage) | Runtime, triggers, packaging, environment, identity |
| S3 (`aws_s3_bucket`) | Storage Account (`azurerm_storage_account`) + container companion | Naming, containers, lifecycle, encryption, public access |
| RDS/PostgreSQL (`aws_rds_cluster` / `aws_db_instance`) | Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server | Version, HA, extensions, backup, firewall, Key Vault password |
| ElastiCache | Azure Cache for Redis | SKU, TLS, private endpoint, auth |
| Route53 zone/record | Azure DNS zone / record | Public vs private, cutover |
| CloudWatch log group | Log Analytics workspace | Retention and diagnostic settings |
| ECS cluster/task | Container Apps environment (+ review) | Whether AKS is a better fit |
| CloudFront | Front Door profile (review-heavy) | Origins, WAF, custom domains |
| SQS (`aws_sqs_queue`) | Service Bus Queue (`azurerm_servicebus_queue`); Storage Queue alternate | FIFO/dead-letter semantics, retry behavior |
| IAM role/policy | Managed identity scaffold + RBAC review notes | Emission is identity-only; operators author RBAC |
| IAM user/group/access key | Entra / non_applicable | Do not recreate static cloud users in azurerm |

## Defaults

- Location: `eastus`
- Resource group pattern: `rg-<group_id>`
- Tags: `generated_by=stackgen-aws-migrator`, `migration_mode=review-candidate`, `standards=caf-waf-opentofu`, `migration_group=<group_id>`
- Networking: VNet/subnet/NSG with deny-Internet inbound baseline when compute/network categories are present; CIDRs are variables for IPAM replacement.
- Identity: user-assigned managed identity scaffold; IAM→RBAC stays review-needed.
- Compute access: SSH public key variable (placeholder must be replaced before apply); password auth disabled.
- SKU posture: low-cost review SKUs unless the source group strongly implies otherwise.
- Module source preference: local Terraform roots under `azure/groups/<group_id>`; replace with AVM/CAF modules later if desired.

## Validation

- Static: `tofu fmt`, `tofu validate` on **all** generated groups (unless an explicit sample override is set).
- Live plan: sampled when `AZURE_LIVE_PLAN_MAX_GROUPS` is set; PR must disclose `planned/total`.
- Never apply migrated Azure resources from this workflow.
- When live plan is required, missing credentials fail validation.
